Tool.
  tool """" KeYmaera X """"
  model """" ArchiveEntry "SMIB negative damping: energy grows (D<0)"

/*
 * Single machine with negative damping D<0 (e.g. grid-following effective
 * negative damping). Hdot = -2D w^2 > 0 whenever w!=0: energy strictly grows.
 * Unlike the two-machine case, there is NO coupling to a passive partner,
 * so the origin cannot be stabilized by any energy-based argument -- the
 * single machine with D<0 is genuinely unstable.
 */
ProgramVariables Real delta; Real w; Real s; Real c; Real h0; End.
Problem
  \forall D \forall K (
    D < 0 & K > 0 & s^2+c^2=1 & h0 = w^2+2*K*(1-c) & w^2 > 0
    ->
    [{delta'=w, w'=-D*w-K*s, s'=c*w, c'=-s*w & s^2+c^2=1 & w^2>0}]
    w^2+2*K*(1-c) >= h0 )
End.
Tactic "Proof" allR(1); allR(1); implyR(1); dI(1) End.
End. """"
  tactic """" (allR(1);allR(1);implyR(1);dI(1)) """"
  proof """"  """"
End.
